\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}
\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}
\usepackage{hyperref}
\begin{document}

\section{Extensions}

Corpus for Phase 1 markdown constructs added after the initial pipeline. Accumulates across tasks — add new sections, don't replace old ones.

\subsection{Task lists (T1.1)}

\begin{itemize}
\item $\square$ unchecked item
\item $\boxtimes$ checked item (lowercase x)
\item $\boxtimes$ checked item (uppercase X)
\item plain bullet item, no checkbox
\end{itemize}

\begin{enumerate}
\item $\square$ first ordered task
\item $\boxtimes$ second ordered task, done
\item plain ordered item
\end{enumerate}

\begin{itemize}
\item $\boxtimes$ checked item with continuation second line of the same item, indented under the checkbox
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Strikethrough (T1.1)}

This is deleted text inside a sentence.

Whole line struck through.

Mixed \textbf{bold and struck together}.

\subsection{Reference links, titles, images (T1.2)}

Inline link with title: \href{https://www.anthropic.com}{Anthropic}.

Reference link: \href{https://example.com/docs}{the docs} explain more.

Collapsed reference: \href{https://example.com/docs-ref}{Docs Ref} also works.

Shortcut reference: \href{https://example.com/docs-ref}{Docs Ref} resolves the same way.

Undefined reference stays literal: [nowhere][missing-ref].

Undefined shortcut stays literal: [Also Missing].

Image with title: [image: a small logo] \url{https://example.com/logo.png}

Reference image: [image: alt text] \url{https://example.com/image.png}

Paren url survives inline: \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haskell_(programming_language)}{Haskell} stays whole.

Paren url by reference: \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haskell_(programming_language)}{the Haskell article}.

Paren-form title: \href{https://example.com/pt}{point here} uses (title) syntax.

\end{document}
